{
  "dom_id": "step-q82289",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -8\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{5} & -2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is a diagonal matrix, hence \n\n$$\n|A|=4\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 3=-24\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has a zero column: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{5} & -2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, only $|B|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
